<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves to system on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves to system on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to add reserves to the banking system via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements on Wednesday, economists said.</p>
<p>The current two-week maintenance period ends on Wednesday and economists said a permanent add to the banking system through the outright purchase of securities -- bills or coupons -- was possible as early this session.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-1/2 percent, right at the Fed's current official target level.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
</text>
